<urn:atm:triage:finding/BB1-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB1-001" ;
  triage:title "String literals split with concat! to defeat the nudge-taxonomy lint and acceptance grep" ;
  triage:description "fenix critical design review, PR #1438 comment https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1438#issuecomment-5648340494 (2026-09-12T20:01:44Z), reviewed at b06b3e262. crates/atm-core/src/doctor/mod.rs:361 (concat!(\"stale_nu\", \"dge_template_override: ...\")), :421-422 (\"disabled_task_nu\", \"dge_template...\"), crates/atm-core/src/team_admin.rs:20 (concat!(\"acknowledge\", \"_task\")), crates/atm/src/commands/teams.rs:897,922. Verified: restoring the plain literal at doctor/mod.rs:361 makes scripts/check-nudge-taxonomy.py fail with a new nudge-family identifier outside the ADR-054 frozen inventory. Sprint doc acceptance 1's grep returns only the parser arm and its test because the two D6 uses are hidden by the concat! split; acceptance 2 (\"just lint nudge-taxonomy passes with no inventory change\") conflicts with D6's finding names. Independently confirmed as QA1-B1/QA1-B2 by quality-mgr's BB1-QA1-1789242600 (Final Quality Report FAIL, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1438#issuecomment-5648365789, 2026-09-12T20:06:32Z), same commit b06b3e262: doctor/mod.rs:394-396 cited there for the second concat! site (fenix's review cited :421-422 for the same pair; both point at the identical split). quality-mgr additionally produced timestamped before/after nudge-taxonomy lint-log proof (.just/logs/20260912190402-nudge-taxonomy.log exit_code 1 before the split, .just/logs/20260912195015-nudge-taxonomy.log exit_code 0 after) confirming the evasion is deliberate, not accidental. Four independent QA reviewers (req-qa, arch-qa, ruthless-boundary-qa, rust-qa-agent) converged on this same finding." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "policy-evasion" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:source "fenix critical review" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-core/src/doctor/mod.rs:361,421-422; crates/atm-core/src/team_admin.rs:20; crates/atm/src/commands/teams.rs:897,922" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T20:01:44Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Lead ruling (fenix): option (a). The two D6 finding codes (stale_nudge_template_override, disabled_task_nudge_template_override) are added to the ADR-054 frozen inventory under the Phase-BB amendment BB.1 already writes; acceptance criterion 1's expected hit list is amended to include the D6 deletion path and its test. The concat! splits are removed. Acceptance 2 is reworded to \"passes with the Phase-BB amendment recorded\". Fix round R1 goes to solar on a top-of-stack worktree above feature/bb1-transition-templates (BB.4 stacks on this branch, unchanged). QA-1 findings from quality-mgr fold into the same round." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB1 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T20:01:44Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/BB1-001/1> ;
  triage:hasResolution <urn:atm:triage:resolution/BB1-001/1> ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-12T22:18:29Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

